{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And YHWH came down to see.</b> There was no need for this — rather, He came to teach judges that they must not condemn the defendant until they see and understand. Midrash of Rabbi Tanchuma." "<b>The children of men.</b> Rather, whose children? Perhaps the children of donkeys and camels? Rather — the children of the first man, who forced the good upon himself and said, ״The woman whom You gave with me״ — these too forced the good upon themselves, to rebel against the One who had bestowed good upon them. And they escaped the Flood."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:17.162487286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}